text.section:
Public adjusters shall ensure that all contracts for their services are in writing and contain the following terms:

Legible full name of the public adjuster signing the contract, as specified in the records of the Commission;


Public adjuster's permanent home state business address and phone number;


Public adjuster's license number, as specified in the records of the Commission;


Title "Public Adjuster Contract";


The insured's full name and street address and the insurance company's name and policy number;


A description of the loss and a description of the location of the loss, if applicable;


A description of services to be provided to the insured by the public adjuster and all terms and conditions of the engagement;


Signatures of the public adjuster and the insured;


The date the contract was signed by the public adjuster and the date the contract was signed by the insured;


Attestation language stating that the public adjuster is fully bonded pursuant to state law;


The full salary, fee, commission, compensation, or other consideration the public adjuster is to receive for services, subject to the provisions of § 38.2-1845.14; and


The right to rescind the contract within three business days after the contract has been signed by the insured or, in the event of a catastrophic disaster, the right to rescind the contract within five business days after the contract has been signed by the insured. Such rescission shall be in writing and mailed or delivered to the public adjuster at the address shown in the contract. Within 15 business days following receipt of the notice to rescind, the public adjuster shall return to the insured anything of value given by the insured under the contract.
